# This file governs a hand-run `docker build` in this directory and nothing
# else. The deploy path in 5.1_deploy.ipynb never reads it: the starter toolkit
# zips the build context with its own bundled dockerignore template regardless
# of how the runtime is configured, and that template excludes `.dockerignore`
# by name, which is why the uploaded source zip carries a copy of this file
# rather than obeying it.
#
# It is kept here for two reasons. The toolkit's `generate_dockerfile` calls
# `_ensure_dockerignore` on the build context during `configure()`, and that
# writes the toolkit's own template copy here whenever this file is absent, so
# deleting it produces an untracked file nobody wrote. Separately, what reaches
# the image is decided by the Dockerfile, which names every file it copies
# instead of using `COPY . .`, so nothing below is what keeps the image clean.

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# Virtual environments and local secrets. `.env` in particular: the Neo4j
# credentials reach the container as launch-time environment variables, and a
# copy baked into the image would outlive the Runtime in ECR.
.venv/
venv/
.env
*.pem
*.key
credentials
.aws/

# Testing and tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage

# Notebooks. The image runs booking_agent.py; the notebook that deploys it has
# no reason to ship inside it.
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Development noise
*.log
*.bak
*.swp
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
.git/

# The shared package reaches the image as the wheel that 5.1_deploy.ipynb
# builds, never as a loose source tree. An earlier flow copied the tree here
# instead, and a leftover copy both bloats the build context and shadows the
# installed package for anything importing `workshop` from this directory.
workshop/

# Starter toolkit state. `.bedrock_agentcore.yaml` records the runtime ID of a
# previous deploy and belongs on the machine doing the deploying, not in the
# image it produces.
.bedrock_agentcore.yaml
.bedrock_agentcore/
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
